## Summary

Clean current-main replacement for the earlier stale observation-oracle proposal #11623.

Implements [AIRROAD-OBSERVATION-ORACLE-001 #11610](https://github.com/Luminous-Dynamics/symthaea/issues/11610) as a standalone, dependency-free Rust reference.

The v0.3.0 source provides:
- typed run manifest with run/asset/configuration/context/procedure/evidence identities and declared time domain;
- SI quantity/unit/sign-convention enums for torque, RPM, thrust, voltage, current, power, temperature, pressure, coolant flow, sound pressure and vibration;
- per-channel calibration certificate, raw-data digest, clock source/uncertainty and quality-coded samples;
- deterministic nearest-actual-sample synchronization at a declared anchor; no interpolation, extrapolation, imputation, hold-last or cross-run join;
- fail-closed calibration/unit/configuration/sequence/time-skew/clock-uncertainty checks;
- typed `MotorMapOperatingPoint` projection from synchronized positive-motoring torque/RPM at the same declared motor-shaft boundary;
- shaft angular velocity and Q×omega power plus a rectangular absolute-bound interval;
- full per-channel timestamp, sample skew, clock, calibration and raw-data lineage;
- 24 synthetic tests and an exact-path format/test/Clippy workflow.

## Verification and claim ceiling

- Rebuilt from the current main head; compare is 5 commits ahead / 0 behind.
- Exact source/manifest/lock/README/workflow fetched back.
- Source contains 24 tests, `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]`, and no lines exceeding 100 columns.
- No local Cargo/rustc/rustfmt is available; compile, formatting execution, tests and Clippy are not claimed as passed.
- Dedicated exact-head workflow must be checked; queued/skipped/pending are not passes.
- Synthetic synchronization and operating-point projection do not calibrate instruments, validate a physical map, establish metrology accuracy, performance, aircraft mission feasibility, safety or airworthiness.

## Intent

Bao goal (owner, standing): "seamlessly allow an agent to drive my actual chrome profile with as few system level permissions like screen recording as possible".

Backlog item: Bao: an idle-ended task's finish line ends in one period, not two"

Found by bao-finish-reason-once (2026-11-11), already on main: an idle end calls workflow.unavailable with AGENT_IDLE_REASON, which already ends in a period, and finish() adds another, so the line ends '..'. Small copy fix; pair it with the next Bao finish-message change.

## What Changed

- `AgentBrowserWorkflow.finish()` drops one trailing period from the failure reason before it adds the sentence period, so an idle end that already ends in a period no longer prints `..`.
- A unit test checks that `AGENT_IDLE_REASON` finishes as one sentence, and that a reason without a period still gets one.

## Risk Assessment

✅ Low: This is a one-line copy fix: before adding the final period, `finish()` now strips one trailing period from the stored reason. The idle path in agent-browser-proxy.ts (line 1421) and `NEWER_TASK_REASON` (line 1401) both now end in one period, and reasons with no period still get one.

## Testing

Drove the real bao mcp server on a throwaway Chrome copy. After the real 10-minute idle timer, the agent-visible finish line and the desktop receipt both ended in one period, not two. A failed save, a blocked open, a newer-task end, and a successful save kept a single period as well.

