This PR introduces new optimization and fixes across the CIR optimizations pipeline:

- Common Subexpression Elimination (`--smr-cse`) using dominance analysis and operation equivalence to safely eliminate redundant memory-effect-free instructions;
- Constant folding (`--smr-const-fold`) with explicit constant evaluation for `cir.binop` operating on `cir.IntAttr` constants inside a fixed-point iteration loop;
- block-level constant propagation (`--smr-const-prop`)  tracking cir.store values to `cir.alloca` locations and replacing subsequent `cir.load` instructions;
- Mem2Reg (`--smr-mem2reg`) with strict single-block eligibility checks to prevent erasing active allocations;
- LICM (`--smr-licm`) was generalized to support `cir::DoWhileOp` alongside `cir::ForOp` using post-order loop traversal.

